{"st":"WI","name":"Wisconsin","seats":[{"census":1840,"seats":2},{"census":1850,"seats":3},{"census":1860,"seats":6},{"census":1870,"seats":8},{"census":1880,"seats":9},{"census":1890,"seats":10},{"census":1900,"seats":11},{"census":1910,"seats":11},{"census":1920,"seats":11},{"census":1930,"seats":10},{"census":1940,"seats":10},{"census":1950,"seats":10},{"census":1960,"seats":10},{"census":1970,"seats":9},{"census":1980,"seats":9},{"census":1990,"seats":9},{"census":2000,"seats":8},{"census":2010,"seats":8},{"census":2020,"seats":8}],"events":[{"congress":30,"year":1848,"kind":"statehood","title":"Statehood","text":"Wisconsin became the 30th state on May 29, 1848. Congress gave it 2 seats in the House until the next apportionment.","sources":["https://www.everycrsreport.com/reports/R47747.html","https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf"]},{"congress":33,"year":1852,"kind":"census","title":"1850 census apportionment","text":"After the 1850 census, Wisconsin's House delegation grew from 2 to 3 seats.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf"]},{"congress":38,"year":1862,"kind":"census","title":"1860 census apportionment","text":"After the 1860 census, Wisconsin's House delegation grew from 3 to 6 seats.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf"]},{"congress":43,"year":1872,"kind":"census","title":"1870 census apportionment","text":"After the 1870 census, Wisconsin's House delegation grew from 6 to 8 seats.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf"]},{"congress":48,"year":1882,"kind":"census","title":"1880 census apportionment","text":"After the 1880 census, Wisconsin's House delegation grew from 8 to 9 seats.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf"]},{"congress":53,"year":1892,"kind":"census","title":"1890 census apportionment","text":"After the 1890 census, Wisconsin's House delegation grew from 9 to 10 seats.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf"]},{"congress":58,"year":1902,"kind":"census","title":"1900 census apportionment","text":"After the 1900 census, Wisconsin's House delegation grew from 10 to 11 seats.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf"]},{"congress":63,"year":1912,"kind":"census","title":"1910 census apportionment","text":"After the 1910 census, Wisconsin kept 11 seats in the House.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf"]},{"congress":73,"year":1932,"kind":"census","title":"1930 census apportionment","text":"After the 1930 census, Wisconsin's House delegation shrank from 11 to 10 seats.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf"]},{"congress":78,"year":1942,"kind":"census","title":"1940 census apportionment","text":"After the 1940 census, Wisconsin kept 10 seats in the House.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf"]},{"congress":83,"year":1952,"kind":"census","title":"1950 census apportionment","text":"After the 1950 census, Wisconsin kept 10 seats in the House.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf"]},{"congress":88,"year":1962,"kind":"census","title":"1960 census apportionment","text":"After the 1960 census, Wisconsin kept 10 seats in the House.","sources":["https://www2.census.gov/decennial/2000/data/apportionment/2000%20PHC3%20Table%203.pdf"]},{"congress":93,"year":1972,"kind":"census","title":"1970 census apportionment","text":"After the 1970 census, Wisconsin's House delegation shrank from 10 to 9 seats. Because districts must have nearly equal populations, the map was redrawn 